  [5] COMMANDS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  --seconds N     stop after N seconds (default: run until Ctrl+C)
  --rate HZ       snapshot rate for console + CSV (default 50)
  --report-ms MS  requested sensor report interval (default 16)
  --log DIR       CSV directory (default: logs next to the executable)
  --no-log        disable CSV logging
  --enumerate     print this report and exit
  --hid-raw       also read one raw input report per HID sensor
  --no-window     do not open the debug fold window
  --manual        start with the estimator in manual mode
  --write-config  write the default config.json next to the executable
  --selftest      run the estimator and safety-gate self tests
  --orientation-demo  native counterpart of testyourdevices.com/gyroscope-test/
  --fold-effect   show the live desktop folding as the lid moves
  --dump-frames   save the captured desktop and rendered frames as BMP
  --allow-display-off  let the display sleep while --fold-effect runs
  --keep-system-awake  block Modern Standby while the lid is shut

  Fold progress is a visual quantity; no physical angle is estimated.


Fold effect armed.
The desktop is left completely untouched at or above the activation
angle.  Close the lid below it and the picture holds the activation
angle -- keystoned and progressively blurred -- while the panel tilts.
Open back above it and the desktop returns untouched.

STOP: press [ESC] or [F10] -- these are read globally, so they work even
      though the overlay holds the screen.  [Q] in this console also works.

  display 1920x1080, 120 dpi -> eye distance 12288 px
  activation 110 deg, blur 65/1000px, darken 0.015, max delta 60 deg
  capture 1920x1080, DXGI_FORMAT 87, overlay 1920x1080
  monitor power on (notify yes), lid switch unknown (notify yes), settle 0.12 s
  claim keep-awake: display yes, system-while-closed yes

Desktop frame captured; the effect is live.


